METHOD: Live render only, against the real running app. Started
`scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8092` (throwaway data copy, 5 seeded
accounts: probe-acct, test-noanchor-acct, usaa-checking, usaa-credit-card,
usaa-health-checking — document order is alphabetical by ID, confirmed via
curl before designing the account-choice for each check). Drove the real
/accounts page with Playwright+chromium (deps already installed in
scratchpad from attempt 1) using real DOM submits (`form.requestSubmit()`
after `form.noValidate = true` to bypass the browser's native required
popup, reproducing exactly what the server sees when a user clears a
pre-filled field and submits) — never simulated HTML. Ran
@axe-core/playwright against the live page in light and `class="dark"`
with every disclosure panel force-opened first (per the rendered-bar
contract). Stopped the verify server afterward. Diff attribution used
`git diff HEAD` scoped to the 4 changed files, plus `git show master:...`
for byte-identical-line checks.

=== SCOPED BEHAVIOR — the four deciding checks ===

1. EDIT-ERROR NO LONGER STRANDED (non-first account) — PASS.
   Cleared Name on `usaa-credit-card` (4th of 5 in document order, not
   first) and submitted. Result: `#acct-edit-panel-usaa-credit-card`
   hidden=false, its toggle button aria-expanded="true";
   `document.activeElement` = `#acct-edit-name-usaa-credit-card`,
   `aria-invalid="true"`, visible=true (real focus, not just DOM
   presence). EVERY OTHER account's edit panel (probe-acct,
   test-noanchor-acct, usaa-checking, usaa-health-checking) stayed
   hidden=true/aria-expanded="false". The Add panel stayed
   hidden=true/aria-expanded="false". This is exactly what attempt 1
   FAILED on (U-2026-09-05n) — now scoped correctly to the one account
   that actually errored, and confirmed on a non-first account so it
   isn't "the first match wins by accident" again.

2. ADD-ERROR STILL WORKS — PASS.
   Opened Add, submitted with a blanked `id`. Add panel
   hidden=false/aria-expanded="true", active element = `#acct-new-id`,
   `aria-invalid="true"`. Every Edit panel stayed collapsed
   (hidden=true/aria-expanded="false").

3. ANCHOR-ERROR ISOLATION — PASS (as literally scoped by the task ask),
   with one pre-existing cross-account defect surfaced as an OBSERVATION.
   Submitted an invalid (blank) `anchor_date` for `usaa-health-checking`
   (last in document order). Result: that account's anchor_date field IS
   flagged `aria-invalid="true"`, and its Edit-settings panel
   (`#acct-edit-panel-usaa-health-checking`) stayed hidden=true — the
   worker's refinement (gating `$editErrored` on ErrorField being "name"
   or "low_balance_threshold" only, never an anchor field) works: an
   anchor error does not pop the unrelated Edit-settings panel open.
   ALL Edit panels and the Add panel stayed collapsed. Both asks in the
   task's check #3 hold.
   OBSERVATION (pre-existing, not this task's regression — see below):
   the anchor_date/anchor_amount template conditions
   (accounts.html:668,682) test only `$root.ErrorField`, never
   `$root.ErrorAccountID` vs `$acct.Account.ID` — unlike the edit-form
   fields, which ruling U-2026-09-05n scoped per-account. Live probe
   confirmed ALL FIVE accounts' anchor_date inputs got
   `aria-invalid="true"` (not just usaa-health-checking's), and
   `document.activeElement` after the swap landed on
   `#acct-anchor-date-probe-acct` (the alphabetically-first account),
   not the account that actually submitted the form. Confirmed via
   `git diff HEAD`/`git show master:...` that these two template lines
   are byte-identical to master, and the JS selector doing the
   first-match-wins pick (`accounts.js:232`,
   `target.querySelector('[data-focus-target]')`) is the same logic
   master's inline script used before U7's extraction — so this
   mis-scoping already existed pre-U12 (anchor forms were never behind
   a disclosure; visibility was never the issue for them). Not a
   regression from this task and outside the ruling n contract (which
   named only the Add/Edit-name/threshold fields, sections 1–5). The
   worker's own new test
   (`TestHandleAddAnchor_InvalidDate_RendererMode_DoesNotOpenEditPanel`)
   and its comment explicitly acknowledge the anchor field itself isn't
   yet scoped ("so the anchor field itself... can eventually be scoped
   correctly too"). Flagging for the backlog, not failing this task on it.

4. NO ERROR → NO PANEL FORCED OPEN — PASS.
   Resubmitted `usaa-checking`'s edit form unchanged (valid). All 5 Edit
   panels and the Add panel stayed hidden=true/aria-expanded="false".
   Active element fell through to `#accounts-list-heading` (the existing
   no-error fallback focus target), not any form field.

=== OTHER REQUIRED CHECKS ===

5. FULL AXE SWEEP, light+dark, all disclosures opened: 0 violations both
   themes (full ruleset, not just color-contrast) — matches attempt 1's
   clean baseline, no regression. Heading order in both themes: H1
   "Accounts" → H2 "Add an account" → H2 "Your accounts" → H3 per account
   → H4 "Matched files" → H4 "Balance anchors" (×5) → H2 "Unassigned
   files". Exactly one H1, no skipped levels.

6. Disclosures are real `<button>`s (confirmed `tagName === 'BUTTON'` for
   the usaa-checking Edit toggle), `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls` present
   and correct, keyboard-operable (Tab to button, Enter opens — panel
   hidden=false, aria-expanded="true", field becomes reachable
   (`offsetParent` truthy); Enter again closes it — hidden=true,
   aria-expanded="false", field unreachable again). Field inside the
   collapsed panel confirmed tab-unreachable (`offsetParent` null) before
   any interaction.

7. `go test ./internal/handlers/accounts/...` → ok. New tests
   (`TestHandleUpdate_EmptyNameSurfaced_SetsErrorAccountID`,
   `TestHandleCreate_EmptyNameSurfaced_ErrorAccountIDEmpty`,
   `TestHandleAddAnchor_InvalidDate_SetsErrorAccountID`,
   `TestHandleUpdate_RendererMode_ErrorRevealsOnlyErroringAccountsPanel`,
   `TestHandleAddAnchor_InvalidDate_RendererMode_DoesNotOpenEditPanel`)
   directly exercise the ErrorAccountID contract server-side, matching
   the live-browser probe above.

=== OBSERVATIONS (not FAILs) ===

- O1 (pre-existing, master-identical): anchor_date/anchor_amount fields
  are not scoped by ErrorAccountID, so an anchor-form error on any one
  account marks every account's corresponding anchor field
  aria-invalid="true" and misdirects focus to the alphabetically-first
  account rather than the one that submitted. Real WCAG 3.3.1 concern,
  but out of this task's ruling-n scope and unaffected by the hidden-panel
  change (anchor forms were never behind a disclosure). Candidate
  follow-up: extend the same `$acct.Account.ID` comparison ruling n
  applied to name/threshold onto anchor_date/anchor_amount.
- O2 (carried from attempt 1, unaffected by this attempt): master-
  identical `acct-edit-name-{{.ID}}` lacks `aria-describedby` to its error
  text.
- O3: `handlers.go`'s `writeJSONError` and the two static error banners in
  accounts.html were converted from hue-literal classes
  (`bg-red-50`/`text-red-700`/etc.) to token classes
  (`bg-negative-soft`/`text-negative`) as part of this diff — consistent
  with the branch's token vocabulary (U6/U7), not a scope violation, and
  covered by the 0-violation axe sweep in both themes.

